In article <78606@bu.edu.bu.edu> vida@bu-geo.bu.edu (Vida Jakabhazy) writes:
>When I want to save the game, typically I will do so just before I go down a
>level.  Invariably when I restart the game, there are 10s of Mordor orcs,
>owlbears, etc either in the same room where I start or in neighboring rooms to
>which my pet(s) will alert me.

This sounds like a definite bug, but I've never run into anything like it here.
A couple things that might help out:  1) What version and patch level are you
currently running?  2) Talk to your games administrator (or local equiv) and
ask if other people have been having similar problems.  3) Ask him/her if 
he/she did anything weird when he/she installed the game.  4) Pray to the
great and fickle computer.  5) Oh - one more thing - what machine type and
operating system are you running it on?

>I know your luck
>decreases by 1 each time you start the game, but I didn't realize that there
>was a concomitant increase in likelihood of immediate death.

An evidently all too common fallacy.  Your luck only decreases by one if/when:
  1) It's a full moon.
  2) It's a game resumed from a previous save.
  3) You save back out.

And no, this doesn't increase your likelihood of immediate death.  :-)

